        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Austerlitz</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">2 December 1805</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">About ten kilometres south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brno">Brno</a>, between Brno and Austerlitz (Slavkov u Brna), then in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a>, now in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The French Empire's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grande-armee">Grande Armée</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> I, some 72,000 men and 157 guns on one account; the Allied army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-i-of-russia">Alexander I</a> and General Kutuzov with Austrian forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Emperor Francis II</a>, about 85,000 men and 318 guns on the same account</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The French broke the Allied centre and routed the Allied army, taking thousands of prisoners. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> agreed a truce on 4 December and signed the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Pressburg</a> on 26 December.</span></div>
